rgument of a predicate whose subject is a SpecificDisease (\"is characterized by,\" \"results in,\" \"secondary to,\" \"due to\"), or a coordinated item in such a list. Extend the span to include its modifiers and prepositional complement (e.g., \"deficiency of norrin,\" not \"deficiency\"). Do not apply this to study variables, methods, or neutral biological processes outside a disease-characterizing clause.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 4218, "output_tokens": 6764, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 5713}, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}